WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.734
The Cannes Film

00:00:00.734 --> 00:00:02.736
Festival is in full swing

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:04.604
on the French Riviera right now.

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:05.805
21 films competing

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:08.041
for the prestigious Palme d'Or prize

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:09.242
and the glamorous event

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:09.943
as usual,

00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:12.746
full of promising blockbuster movies

00:00:12.746 --> 00:00:14.147
up and coming talent.

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:16.282
And, of course, Hollywood A-listers

00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:18.218
like Leonardo DiCaprio,

00:00:18.218 --> 00:00:20.453
Michael Douglas, Natalie Portman.

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:22.922
And there is a hint of controversy

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:23.656
as well

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:25.258
over the choice of the film

00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:27.327
that kicked off the festival.

00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:29.629
And I'm delighted now to welcome

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:30.930
from Cannes,

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:31.765
Scott Roxborough,

00:00:31.765 --> 00:00:33.166
the Hollywood Reporter's

00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:34.534
Europe bureau chief.

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:36.603
Scott, so lovely to reconnect with you.

00:00:36.803 --> 00:00:38.405
The Cannes Film Festival

00:00:38.405 --> 00:00:39.539
kicked off this week

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:42.108
and it got off to a controversial start.

00:00:42.509 --> 00:00:44.711
Why are some people upset?

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:46.112
Yeah. Hi. Hi.

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:47.347
Good to see you.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:48.148
Yeah,

00:00:48.148 --> 00:00:50.550
the festival was a bit controversial

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.484
this year, particularly

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:53.820
because the opening film John de Berry,

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.588
which is a French film about

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:57.991
the

00:00:58.458 --> 00:01:00.860
sort of the end of the

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:02.996
French royal family.

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:05.465
But the controversy was around

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:08.101
who was playing King Louis, which is

00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:09.135
it was

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:11.371
Johnny Depp was cast for the lead role.

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:12.705
And of course, Johnny Depp

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:14.841
is a very controversial figure now

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:17.444
due to his very public legal disputes

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:18.912
with his ex-wife.

00:01:18.912 --> 00:01:21.281
Amber Heard and allegations of abuse

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:22.549
against him.

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:23.883
It didn't seem to affect the way

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:25.585
that fans reacted to him.

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:28.021
And the French audiences never really

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:30.356
turned against Johnny Depp.

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:32.659
And many people saw his arrival here

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:34.260
and his presentation of this film

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:34.761
as an

00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:36.763
as a as a sort of return

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:37.997
to the spotlight.

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:39.632
But a definitely was a lot of controversy

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:40.700
around this

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:42.302
in choosing this film to open the Cannes

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:43.103
Film Festival

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:45.105
and a lot of questions being asked

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:47.373
as to why they actually picked it.

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:48.241
And incidentally,

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:50.610
of course, that film directed by a woman.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:51.978
And speaking of women,

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:52.812
we're seeing more

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:55.081
and more filmmakers in competition

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:56.749
at the Film Festival of Women,

00:01:56.749 --> 00:01:58.852
but nowhere near parity.

00:01:58.852 --> 00:02:00.553
Give us a sense of what role

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:02.722
women play in this festival.

00:02:02.722 --> 00:02:05.959
How are organizers dealing with criticism

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:06.993
leveled at them

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:08.027
that there are not enough

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:10.163
female filmmakers at Cannes?

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:11.831
Do you see things changing

00:02:13.733 --> 00:02:14.267
Well,

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:16.302
for cans level, things have changed

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:17.137
quite a bit.

00:02:17.137 --> 00:02:18.638
There are six

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:21.207
women in competition, female directors

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:22.475
with films and competition.

00:02:22.475 --> 00:02:24.010
That's the most there's ever been.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:24.811
But as you said, it's

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:25.578
nowhere near parity.

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:26.813
It's just about 30%,

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:29.382
which is nowhere near 50.

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:31.718
The on on a sort of structural

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:32.619
level, Cannes has done

00:02:32.619 --> 00:02:34.187
a few things as well.

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:35.588
The president of the Cannes

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:36.356
Film Festival,

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:38.858
The Big Boss, is a woman erotic novel.

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:39.726
The first time

00:02:39.726 --> 00:02:41.461
a woman has had that position.

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:42.962
And she's been very vocal

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:45.565
about trying to get through gender parity

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:47.367
within the festival,

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:48.801
but they still got a long way to go.

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:49.335
I mean, I remember

00:02:49.335 --> 00:02:50.103
just a couple of years

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:51.671
ago, Cannes was promising

00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:53.339
to reach 50% parity

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:54.574
in terms of female directors

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:56.743
in competition by 20, 20.

00:02:56.743 --> 00:02:58.211
It's now, of course, 20, 23.

00:02:58.211 --> 00:03:00.313
And we're still a long way from that.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.048
And it's trying to make progress

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:03.816
but a lot of people are saying it's

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:05.919
not doing nearly enough.

00:03:05.919 --> 00:03:08.254
Now, Scott can be incredibly glamorous.

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:09.222
You got beautiful

00:03:09.222 --> 00:03:10.089
people booted

00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:12.358
and suited on the Red carpet,

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:14.160
a gorgeous gowns

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.329
going up those famous stairs.

00:03:16.329 --> 00:03:18.131
But the film industry, on a serious

00:03:18.131 --> 00:03:19.299
note, is going through

00:03:19.299 --> 00:03:21.267
a very challenging time.

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:21.534
You know,

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:23.002
how do you see that

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:24.604
displayed at the festival?

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:25.738
What kind of role does it play?

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:27.907
Yeah, it plays a

00:03:27.907 --> 00:03:28.374
huge role

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:29.809
because the film industry

00:03:29.809 --> 00:03:32.078
is one of the reasons that Cannes exists.

00:03:32.078 --> 00:03:33.580
It's not just a big film festival.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:34.981
It's also a huge film market

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:36.449
where films are bought and sold.

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:36.983
And so

00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:37.884
whatever is happening

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:39.052
in the international film industry,

00:03:39.052 --> 00:03:40.954
you feel it here in in Cannes,

00:03:40.954 --> 00:03:41.588
and of course,

00:03:41.588 --> 00:03:42.722
the big issue on everyone's mind

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:45.024
right now is the ongoing writers' strike.

00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:47.060
The Hollywood writers are on strike.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:48.027
That means no

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:50.129
new films are being written.

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:51.264
That's having an impact here.

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:52.899
People are really concerned

00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:54.300
that not just the writers,

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:55.768
but very soon the directors,

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:56.236
the Directors

00:03:56.236 --> 00:03:57.971
Guild is also negotiating a contract.

00:03:57.971 --> 00:04:00.907
And SAG the Screen Actors Guild

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:02.342
could also soon be on strike.

00:04:02.342 --> 00:04:04.611
If that happens, the entire film industry

00:04:04.611 --> 00:04:05.912
in Hollywood shuts down

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:07.447
and that will have a knock on effect

00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:08.281
on the rest of the world.

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:09.849
So although everyone's celebrating

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:11.851
here, cinema in Cannes,

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:13.553
walking those red carpet steps and

00:04:13.553 --> 00:04:15.288
and having a great time,

00:04:15.288 --> 00:04:16.256
everyone's concerned

00:04:16.256 --> 00:04:17.624
that the party could be over

00:04:17.624 --> 00:04:18.992
very, very soon.

00:04:18.992 --> 00:04:20.660
And my final question to you, Scott,

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:22.862
what are the hottest movies so far?

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:24.897
And of the films that you did see,

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:26.566
which is the best film in Cannes

00:04:26.566 --> 00:04:27.600
that we should all check out?

00:04:29.202 --> 00:04:29.769
Yeah, well, we had a

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:30.870
couple of sort of big Hollywood

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:31.871
films screened here.

00:04:31.871 --> 00:04:32.839
Probably the funnest

00:04:32.839 --> 00:04:34.040
was the new Indiana Jones

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:35.008
film, Indiana Jones

00:04:35.008 --> 00:04:36.209
on the Dial of Destiny.

00:04:36.209 --> 00:04:37.377
Basically everything you'd want

00:04:37.377 --> 00:04:39.078
from an Indiana Jones movie,

00:04:39.078 --> 00:04:40.113
the fifth entry

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:41.581
with Harrison Ford and the last.

00:04:41.581 --> 00:04:42.482
He's 80 years old,

00:04:42.482 --> 00:04:43.383
so he won't be coming back

00:04:43.383 --> 00:04:45.184
for another Indiana Jones films.

00:04:45.184 --> 00:04:45.752
That was a great

00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:47.020
sort of entertaining movie.

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:48.354
But in terms of the film

00:04:48.354 --> 00:04:50.023
that I think could win the Palme d'Or

00:04:50.023 --> 00:04:51.057
and definitely the best film

00:04:51.057 --> 00:04:51.824
I've seen year,

00:04:51.824 --> 00:04:53.826
I'd have to go with The Zone of Interest,

00:04:53.826 --> 00:04:56.262
which is a very tough film

00:04:56.262 --> 00:04:58.364
set in Auschwitz about the Holocaust

00:04:58.364 --> 00:04:59.132
from British director

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:00.366
Jonathan Glazer,

00:05:00.366 --> 00:05:02.502
but a German, a language movie.

00:05:03.002 --> 00:05:04.370
And it's very difficult to describe

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.205
in a short one or two sentences,

00:05:06.205 --> 00:05:08.241
but it's just incredibly powerful and

00:05:08.908 --> 00:05:09.842
moving and

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:12.278
and and wrenching really emotionally,

00:05:12.278 --> 00:05:12.945
but done in a way

00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:14.514
that I don't think I've ever seen

00:05:14.514 --> 00:05:16.883
before in a Holocaust movie.

00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:19.118
It's definitely sort of breaks new ground

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:20.620
for tackling the subject.

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:22.488
I think it probably will be rewarded

00:05:22.488 --> 00:05:23.189
next week

00:05:23.189 --> 00:05:25.425
come the come the Cannes Palme d'Or.

00:05:26.059 --> 00:05:26.526
All right.

00:05:26.526 --> 00:05:27.760
Scott Roxborough,

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:29.262
great catching up with you.

00:05:29.262 --> 00:05:30.863
Thank you so much for getting up so early

00:05:30.863 --> 00:05:31.264
for us.

00:05:31.264 --> 00:05:32.632
We greatly appreciate it. Thank you,

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:34.267
Robert.

00:05:34.367 --> 00:05:34.600
All right.

